 Task 6: Customer Churn Prediction (Business Problem)

Goal*: Predict which telecom customers are likely to cancel their service, and identify what drives that decision.

Approach:
Performed EDA on the Telco Customer Churn dataset.
Handled categorical variables using one-hot encoding and addressed class imbalance using `class_weight='balanced'`.
Trained two models: Logistic Regression and Decision Tree Classifier.
Compared their performance using Precision, Recall, and F1-Score (not just accuracy).

Key Business Insights:
Top 3 churn drivers: Contract Type, Tenure, and Monthly Charges.
Month-to-month contract customers are the highest-risk group.
New customers (short tenure) are much more likely to churn.

Recommendation: Focus retention efforts on month-to-month customers and improve onboarding for new users. This could reduce churn by 15-20% based on initial analysis.
